 "type": "hazard",
 "summary": "finalize_once() guard fails when the ledger POST succeeds but the response is lost",
 "content": "`finalize_once()` in src/billing/invoices.py only skips if `invoice.ledger_ref` is set. `ledger_ref` is assigned after the response comes back. If the ledger accepts the POST but the client times out (timeout=10) or the process dies before the assignment, `ledger_ref` stays None and a later `finalize_once()` posts again. The check-then-post also has no lock, so two concurrent callers can both post. A real fix needs an idempotency key sent to the ledger (e.g. invoice.id), not just the local guard. Also, nothing in invoices.py persists `ledger_ref` to the DB column added in migrations/0003; callers have to save it.",
 "physical": [
  "src/billing/invoices.py"
 ],
 "tags": [
  "billing",
  "ledger"
 ],
 "confidence": 0.7,
